From 095d75424e9c9c41d81439c711489acdab615633 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:33:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 04/11] Ray query passes: bind 4 descriptor sets instead of 9

Mobile GPUs can bind few descriptor sets at once (Adreno 7xx: 8, with
Turnip 7; Adreno 6xx and others: 4), and the path tracer needed 9, so
pipeline layout creation would fail on Android.

The small sets (TLAS, global uniform, blue noise, light sources,
cubemaps, render cubemap) are now copied each frame into one combined
set with vkCopyDescriptorSet; framebuffers, vertex data and bindless
textures stay as they are. Set/binding numbers are shared through
DESC_SET_RQ_* / BINDING_RQ_* in GenerateShaderCommon.py, and the ray
query shaders opt in with DESC_SET_RAY_QUERY_COMBINED, which remaps
the bindings in ShaderCommonGLSLFunc.h. Other passes are unchanged.

Rendering is pixel-identical to the original ray tracing pipeline on
lavapipe (60-frame test scene with alpha-tested, mirror and glass
geometry), and the maxBoundDescriptorSets validation error is gone.
